{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786440153,"nonce":"HX6rkZo68pO6yNMLZ1XfbVjcHOI=","message":"Done. **Both coverage ratchets are at zero**, and nothing was exempted — `notYetCovered` is still an empty map, so no operation was excused rather than covered.\n\n```\n--- PASS: TestEveryOperationIsNamedByATest              (was 22 unnamed)\n--- PASS: TestEveryOperationWithAPathIdIsTenantProbed   (was 17 unprobed)\n--- PASS: TestTheExemptionListNamesRealOperations\n```\n\nThe real operation count is **85**, not 71.\n\nNew files: `internal/alerts/api/alerts_contract_test.go` (13 newly-named operations and 13 of the 17 tenant probes), `internal/rules/api/rules_contract_test.go`, `internal/identity/api/identity_contract_test.go`, `internal/enrichment/api/enrichers_contract_test.go`, alongside the ingestion, drill, notification, silences, sources, grouping, streaming and stats contract tests landed earlier in the session.\n\nEvery shape assertion is `schema.Assert`/`AssertProblem`/`AssertNoBody` against `openapi.yaml` and every request fixture goes through `schema.AssertRequest` — **no hand-restated bodies anywhere**, which was the point: a hand-written expectation is a second copy of the contract and it drifts exactly the way the DTOs did. Branch coverage goes well past the happy path: 403 for a machine principal on all five human verbs, 404 via a 13-row tenant table plus non-UUID and nil-UUID ids, 412 preconditions on ack/unack/snooze/unsnooze, 422 with `violations[]` and code for snooze bounds and both/neither spellings, blank comments, bad label names and bad event types, 400 for `empty_body` and `unknown_parameter`, 401 on every route, and 500 on the two sub-reads that must fail loudly rather than render.\n\n**Five divergences found. The first is a real defect on a credential-minting endpoint:**\n\n1. ⭐ **`Idempotency-Key` is declared in the contract and read by nothing.** It is declared on `createApiToken`/`revokeApiToken`, but `internal/identity/api/tokens.go` never reads it. Verified by execution: two POSTs carrying the same key mint **two live PATs** — one of whose secrets the client never saw, since only the second response is returned. A retry after a timeout silently leaves a credential nobody knows about. Pinned as `TestBUG_ARetriedCreateApiTokenWithTheSameIdempotencyKeyMintsASecondCredential`.\n2. **`getAlertRuleHistory` diffs against the wrong snapshot.** The handler builds `change` from `DiffSince(bound.Fingerprint)` — this episode's snapshot against the NEWEST version — but `RuleChangeDTO` is defined as the diff between the PREVIOUS occurrence's snapshot and this one. So an episode that fired under the newest rule text reports `change: null` instead of the edit that preceded it, which is precisely the drift signal ADR 0009 exists to surface. Needs an `AlertReader` port change rather than a handler tweak.\n3. **Undeclared 400s**: `getRuleSnapshot`, `getOccurrenceRule`, `getAlertRuleHistory` and `listEnrichers` all answer `400 unknown_parameter` per SPEC §E.3 but declare no 400 response.\n4. **A fixture the repository could never produce**, caught by the schema on first run: a test's `delivery.LastErrorClass` was `\"auth\"`, outside the contract's closed enum. Fixed to `auth_expired`.\n5. Observation, not pinned: `getCurrentPrincipal` and `getOrgSettings` never build `httpx.Params`, so an unknown query parameter is silently ignored rather than refused. Consistent with the contract as written and cannot return wrong rows, but inconsistent with §E.3.\n\nNote for whoever touches lint next: `internal/alerts/api/world_test.go` was briefly deleted as `unused` mid-session and restored — it is now the shared harness for eighteen operations, so an `unused` sweep must not remove it again.","files":null}]}